      "content": "Interest: Conversational German — wants to learn: Get conversational in German
Domain: language

Current routine:
- next: plain-explainer (Plain-English Explainer) ON, guided-discovery (Guided Discovery) ON, watch-along (Watch Along) ON, guided-reading (Guided Reading) ON, worked-example (Worked Example) ON, mini-case (Mini Case) ON, big-picture-map (Big Picture Map) off
- strengthen: retrieval-quiz (Quick Retrieval) ON, explain-back (Explain It Back) ON, focused-drill (Focused Drill) ON, faded-example (Complete the Example) ON, spot-the-error (Spot the Error) ON, compare-contrast (Compare & Contrast) ON, notice-training (Noticing Reps) ON, mixed-review (Mixed Review) off
- go_further: put-to-work (Put It to Work) ON, make-something (Make Something Small) ON, teach-back (Teach It Forward) ON, scenario-challenge (Scenario Challenge) ON, in-the-wild (In the Wild) ON, dig-deeper (Dig Deeper) ON, connect-ideas (Connect Ideas) ON

Notes they have already set:
- Prefers speaking practice over grammar drills

Their request: Less grammar drilling please — I'd rather spend the time actually saying and writing sentences, and I like the video ones.",
      "role": "user",
    },
  ],
  "system": [
    {
      "cache": true,
      "text": "You are the generation engine inside thinkering, a local-first mobile app that helps adults make steady, real progress on things they want to learn — in the time they actually have (5–15 minute sessions).

How the product works: an Interest is something the user wants to learn. Its Path is an ordered list of Goals — each one a well-scoped unit teachable in one session, carrying named concepts and skills. Each day the Today tab offers three lanes: Next (introduce a new goal), Strengthen (consolidate via retrieval and practice), and Go further (apply learning to the user's life, or extend it deeper/wider). Completing an activity advances the goal's status: not_started → introduced → strengthened → applied. Activities are multi-page interactive documents built from a library of learning strategies; a deterministic scheduler picks the goals — you never decide scheduling, only content.

